3. Strings vs. Bytes (encode() & decode())
Encoding (.encode()): Converts internal Python Unicode strings into a stream of UTF-8 byte arrays to transmit over the network.

Decoding (.decode()): Converts incoming network byte streams back into readable Python text strings.

